{"id":"continuum","corpus":"aws","title":"AWS Continuum","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/continuum/latest/userguide/what-is-continuum.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"AWS Continuum"},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS Continuum helps enterprises defend against security exposures at machine speed. AWS Continuum continuously prioritizes security exposures, correlating vulnerabilities, threats, and exploit activity. It automatically remediates high-priority exposures based on business risk."},{"kind":"p","text":"Frontier AI models have given attackers new capabilities, such as generating complex exploits from vulnerability disclosures in minutes rather than hours. Security teams already cannot keep up with the volume of findings across their environments, and that volume is now accelerating. Prioritizing which findings matter requires understanding which systems are business-critical, how identities connect to sensitive data, and what an attacker can realistically reach."},{"kind":"p","text":"With AWS Continuum, you can discover, prioritize, validate, and remediate vulnerabilities at machine speed. AWS Continuum for code vulnerabilities focuses on finding, validating, and remediating first-party code vulnerabilities. It integrates with GitHub and Amazon S3 for code and context."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Features of AWS Continuum"},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS Continuum provides the following features."},{"kind":"p","text":"Code vulnerabilities"},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS Continuum finds, validates, and remediates first-party code vulnerabilities across your repositories and uploaded code. For more information, see Code vulnerabilities."},{"kind":"p","text":"Penetration testing"},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS Continuum continuously validates exploitability against your environment. For more information, see Perform a penetration test in the AWS Security Agent User Guide."},{"kind":"p","text":"Threat modeling"},{"kind":"p","tex